  "query_preview": "period of deep layer dry and stable conditions under strong \nsubsidence as ridging dominates throughout the column. No \nprecipitation is forecast through the upcoming weekend as upper \nridging maintains control. Temperatures still edged slightly on the \ncooler side of average Thursday and Friday, before a moderating \nthermal profile under full insolation and increasing thicknesses \nlift highs back into the lower 70s by this weekend. Radiational \ncooling under clear skies will keep overnight lows generally in the \nmid to upper 40s. Next meaningful chance of rain unlikely to come \nuntil at least the middle of next week.",
